<Layout title="A small bird. A very big idea. — The Gubbi">
<section class="story-hero wrap"><h1>Some things<br/>deserve to <span class="serif">stay.</span></h1><div><img src="/brand/gubbi-flower.svg" alt="" width="150" height="150"/><p>Gubbi means sparrow in Kannada.<br/>Small. Familiar. Easy to miss.<br/>Until it isn’t there.</p></div></section>
<section class="story-opening"><div class="wrap"><h2>A little piece of where<br/>we <span class="serif">come from.</span></h2><p>Cities change. We know. But somewhere between the next flyover and the next identical café, we started wondering: what happens to all the little things that make a place feel like itself?</p></div></section>
<section class="editorial-row wrap"><div><h2>The things<br/>between the<br/><span class="serif">landmarks.</span></h2><p>Not just the skyline. The ride home. The shared joke. The particular chaos that makes you say, “Only in Bengaluru.”</p><p>We want to make objects about those things. Small enough for a desk. Specific enough to start a conversation.</p><a href="/shop" class="text-link">Meet the first characters <Icon/></a></div><div class="editorial-photo"><ProductCrop position="p-6" alt="Namma Metro Sprint object concept"/><p>Some local rituals happen at full sprint.</p></div></section>
<section class="story-principle wrap"><span>THE IDEA IS SIMPLE</span><h2>Keep the craft.<br/>Change the <span class="serif">conversation.</span></h2><div><p>We’re beginning with Channapatna’s turned-wood tradition: a craft with its own colour, tactility and character. Our ambition is to bring it into the lives we’re actually living.</p><p>These first six pieces are concepts. The next chapter is prototypes, time with makers, and learning what the material wants to be. We’ll share the people and process when we can show them properly.</p></div><a class="text-link" href="/philosophy">The way we want to make <Icon/></a></section>
<section class="two-worlds"><div class="wrap"><h2>One Gubbi.<br/><span class="serif">Two ways in.</span></h2><div><a href="/shop"><h3>Take a little thing home.</h3><p>That’s this place. Objects with local stories and very distinct personalities.</p><span>The Gubbi <Icon/></span></a><a href="https://gubbiartclub.com"><h3>Make a little thing yourself.</h3><p>Art workshops for curious hands. Same spirit, with a little more paint on your clothes.</p><span>Gubbi Art Club <Icon/></span></a></div></div></section>
</Layout>
